# Snowboard DePIN — Solana / Anchor Development Rules

## Stack
- Solana programs: Rust + Anchor framework (latest stable 0.30.x)
- Client SDK: `@coral-xyz/anchor` + `@solana/web3.js`
- Token standard: SPL Token / Token-2022 for $FUSION rewards
- Tests: Anchor TypeScript tests in `tests/`

## Anchor Conventions
- Program ID lives in `declare_id!()` and `Anchor.toml`; keep them in sync
- Use PDAs with canonical seeds documented in account structs (`#[account(seeds = [...], bump)]`)
- Prefer `init` / `init_if_needed` over manual account creation in clients
- All instructions must validate signers, owners, and account constraints in `#[derive(Accounts)]`
- Use `#[account(mut)]` only where state or lamports actually change
- Return typed errors via `#[error_code]` enum — never `require!` with raw strings in production paths

## Security (DePIN-specific)
- Hardware telemetry MUST be verified via Ed25519 precompile (`Ed25519Program`) in the same transaction; introspect with `instructions` sysvar
- Enforce replay protection: monotonic nonce or slot-bound telemetry records
- Device registration binds an Ed25519 public key to an on-chain `Device` PDA — never trust unsigned payloads
- Treasury Vault transfers require PDA signer seeds; cap per-epoch rewards in `GlobalConfig`
- Validate mint, vault authority, and recipient ATA against `GlobalConfig` on every payout

## Code Style
- One instruction handler per `pub fn` in `#[program]` module
- Account structs grouped by instruction; shared types in `state/` module if file grows
- Constants (seeds, max sizes) at module top: `pub const DEVICE_SEED: &[u8] = b"device";`
- Keep `lib.rs` focused; extract helpers (e.g. `verify_ed25519_ix`) to `utils/` when > ~400 lines

## Build & Deploy
```bash
anchor build          # compile program + generate IDL
anchor test           # local validator tests
anchor deploy --provider.cluster devnet
```

## Client Integration
- Deserialize accounts with generated IDL types
- Ed25519 verify ix must precede `submit_telemetry` in the transaction
- Use `connection.getLatestBlockhash()` and confirm with `confirmed` commitment

## Do NOT
- Store private keys or mnemonics in repo
- Skip signer checks on owner/admin paths
- Transfer rewards without checking treasury balance and rate limits
- Use unchecked arithmetic for token amounts — use `checked_mul` / `checked_add`
